I have been playing with a previous commit of your branch: e9465d16bea7aea78f842d856dac099f721a3772
and built with -DUSE_ATOMIC_FALLBACKS I also encountered an assertion.  I had made basically the same
mistake.  It is a wrong expectation, in the debug assert, because the first qp_idx is completely random,
only then the users count of this possibly retired QP is incremented, it can later be allocated and in that moment
there is a small chance that the qp_idx matches the reader_idx.  When you look again at the users_count
it will no longer be RETIRED, it might in worst case happen that it is OBTAINED and the reader_idx is incremented,
but now the writers should be waiting, and cannot miss the lock.
So I did this to your previous commit
```
diff --git a/crypto/threads_pthread.c b/crypto/threads_pthread.c
index 53f8a6e1e7..d65e2b6095 100644
--- a/crypto/threads_pthread.c
